# Dependencies
node_modules/
app/node_modules/

# Env / secrets (Turso URL + auth token live here)
.env
.env.local
app/.env

# Local Turso database + sync engine sidecar files (scenario.db-info, -wal, etc)
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/

# Build output
out/
dist/
app/out/
app/dist/

# Generated icon artifacts. icon.ico IS tracked: make-tauri-icons.mjs copies it
# to src-tauri/icons/icon.ico, which tauri.conf.json lists as the window and
# installer icon, and `sharp` is not installed, so it cannot be regenerated on
# demand. The 4K icon.png IS regenerable from icon-source.png via
# app/build/make-icon.mjs, so it stays out of history.
app/build/icon.png
app/build/_preview.png

# Logs / OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Archives / generated design output (e.g. Stitch UI exports)
*.zip
stitch_*/

# Claude config (not version-controlled)
.claude/

# Project instruction file: authority #1, but local-only and never published.
# Same rule as docs/memory/ below -- it does not survive a clone.
CLAUDE.md

# Path-keyed memory: local working copy, not published
docs/memory/

# Rust build output. `target` is the MSVC build dir (the default toolchain);
# `target-gnu` is the legacy GNU one (see .cargo/config.toml). Both are
# DIRECTORY JUNCTIONS into C:/build/vessel, so the multi-GB build output sits
# outside the OneDrive-synced tree. Recreate with `New-Item -ItemType Junction`
# after a fresh clone; nothing in the build cares that they are junctions.
/target/
/target-gnu/
/src-tauri/target/
# Regenerated by tauri-build on every build.
/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Local character-testing scratch. Never published; not part of the app.
# No trailing slash: this is a FILE, not a directory. Matches either way if it
# later becomes a folder.
/Character_Test

# The summariser A/B harness, its prompt script and its run transcripts, all
# local-only. The content is the reason: `ab/script.json` holds 1,000 explicit
# prompts and the JSONLs hold ~1,000 explicit model replies, which is exactly
# what those runs exercise, and this repo is public.
#
# The harness goes with them rather than being published alone, because it
# `include_str!`s `ab/facts.json` and `ab/script.json` - a COMPILE-TIME include,
# so shipping the .rs without the data breaks `cargo build --examples` on a
# fresh clone instead of merely leaving it unrunnable.
#
# Nothing is lost by this: what the runs established is written up as
# measurements in docs/MASTER.md and docs/decisions/0003, which is the part a
# clone needs. See the summariser-ab-2000 and llama-local-ab-run-state notes in
# docs/memory/ for the run state itself.
/docs/measurements/
/src-core/examples/ab/
/src-core/examples/summariser-ab.rs
